athena-installer-data (1.2.0) thor; urgency=low

  * COMP-01f Phase 1 (revised) — fix the override mechanism.
    First attempt (1.1.0) shipped debconf-overrides.dat with type=string
    set-selections for `debian-installer/main-menu-title`, but that
    template is type=text — set-selections is a no-op on text/note
    templates because the rendered string IS the Description field,
    not a separate settable value.  Result on first install: hooks
    fired (syslog confirmed S40 applied 72 lines) but main-menu screen
    still said "Debian Installer Main menu".
    .
    Fix: split overrides into two mechanisms keyed by template type.
    - data/athena-overrides.templates (lands at /usr/share/athena-
      installer-data/) re-declares type=text templates with our
      Description.  Loaded via `debconf-loadtemplate` in S40 AFTER
      S20templates has already loaded main-menu's templates, so the
      LAST load wins on path-key conflict.
    - data/debconf-overrides.dat now only holds VALUE overrides
      (type=string/boolean/select).  Currently just netcfg/get_hostname.
    - data/S40-athena-branding rewritten to apply both mechanisms:
      debconf-loadtemplate first, then debconf-set-selections.

  * COMP-01f Phase 2 — REMOVED.  The S35-athena-palette + palette.athena
    mechanism from 1.1.0 was confirmed broken on first install: the
    hook fires (syslog confirms NEWT_COLORS_FILE=/etc/newt/palette.athena
    was exported) but the palette doesn't apply.  Two stacking reasons:
    (a) rootskel execs startup scripts as children rather than sourcing
    them, so the export dies with S35's shell; (b) cdebconf-newt has
    its own internal palette logic and doesn't honour newt's
    NEWT_COLORS / NEWT_COLORS_FILE env vars regardless.  Per
    Principle P1 we will NOT patch cdebconf-newt source — colour
    rebrand is documented as irreducible residue in
    docs/branding-methodology.md § 7 and accepted.

 -- Athena Linux <athena@local>  Thu, 22 May 2026 01:45:00 +0000

athena-installer-data (1.1.0) thor; urgency=low

  * COMP-01f Phase 1: ship debconf-overrides + startup hook for
    installer-visible string rebrand (no upstream source patches).
    - data/debconf-overrides.dat (lands at /usr/share/athena-installer-
      data/debconf-overrides.dat) holds the d-i template override
      lines in debconf-set-selections format.  Currently overrides
      main-menu-title, generic title, exit-confirmation title,
      cdebconf/distribution, and netcfg/get_hostname.  Extend
      incrementally as more visible strings surface.
    - data/S40-athena-branding (lands at /lib/debian-installer-
      startup.d/S40-athena-branding, +x) applies the overrides via
      debconf-set-selections BEFORE main-menu (S60) so every consumer
      udeb sees the overridden values.  Soft-fails on missing file
      or apply error (cosmetic-only — don't block install).

  * COMP-01f Phase 2: ship cdebconf-newt colour palette + apply hook.
    Folded into the same udeb (rather than a separate athena-
    installer-theme-udeb) per docs/branding-methodology.md — the
    Devuan pattern (single companion udeb for both identity strings
    and visual theme) suits a 2-file delta better than the Kali
    pattern (separate themes pkg) which exists to support multiple
    flavour themes.  If we later want flavour-themes, split out.
    - data/palette.athena (lands at /etc/newt/palette.athena) holds
      the newt colour palette: deep blue + bright-blue accents
      matching the Aegis SVG runtime wallpaper.
    - data/S35-athena-palette (lands at /lib/debian-installer-
      startup.d/S35-athena-palette, +x) exports NEWT_COLORS_FILE so
      cdebconf-newt picks up the palette before opening any dialog.
      Runs before S40 (debconf overrides) and S60 (main-menu).

  * Pattern source: Kali / Devuan / Parrot all use a companion udeb
    + debconf-overrides + early startup hook shape, documented in
    docs/branding-methodology.md § 3.  Per Principle P1 we
    explicitly REJECT patching cdebconf or cdrom-detect source for
    branding strings — every upstream point release would force a
    patch refresh.  The irreducible residue (priority sigils baked
    into cdebconf-newt, syslog messages baked into cdrom-detect) is
    catalogued in § 7 and accepted.

 -- Athena Linux <athena@local>  Thu, 22 May 2026 00:45:00 +0000

athena-installer-data (1.0.1) thor; urgency=low

  * FORK-01 Step 4: migrate runtime dirs + release files + debootstrap
    codename symlink from installer_chroot.py Python helpers.
    - Ship /tmp, /var/tmp, /root via debian/dirs (trust dh_fixperms
      for /tmp + /var/tmp = 1777; /root gets debhelper default 0755).
    - Ship /etc/lsb-release + /etc/default-release with codename
      substituted at build time from ATHENA_CODENAME env var.
    - Ship /usr/share/debootstrap/scripts/${codename} as symlink to
      sid (same pattern debootstrap-udeb uses for bookworm/sid/kali).
  * FORK-01 Step 3 (delivered at 1.0.0, documented here for clarity):
    /var/lib/dpkg/info/athena-stubs.templates ships the mirror/protocol
    stub that lets bootstrap-base.postinst's db_get succeed.

